Local modification for ttree:
  src/os/mod.rs adds a `target_os = "android"` arm, mapping android to the
  existing `linux` module so the crate compiles for `aarch64-linux-android`
  (upstream 0.2.2 has no android arm). This is a compile-only shim: ttree never
  exercises portable-pty's serial path, so the (linux-shaped, Bionic-incorrect)
  layout is dead code that is dropped by `--gc-sections`. See
  ../../docs/android-termux-build.md for the full rationale.
